## METRO 2039 at a glance

METRO 2039 is the next main game in 4A Games' METRO series, published by Deep Silver. It is a single-player first-person shooter set in post-apocalyptic Moscow. Both the official Steam listing and Deep Silver's METRO 2039 site give the same release day: **4 February 2027**, checked 26 November 2026.

## What we know so far

- **Developer:** 4A Games. **Publisher:** Deep Silver.
- **Release date:** 4 February 2027, on Steam and on the official site.
- **Platforms:** the official FAQ says the game launches on the same day on PlayStation 5, Xbox Series X|S and PC (Steam, the Epic Games Store and Xbox on PC).
- **Price on Steam (US):** $69.99 for the standard edition.
- **Editions:** the official site lists a Standard edition, a Deluxe edition (digital or physical) and a physical Collector's edition. Deluxe adds a Story Expansion DLC, a digital soundtrack and an art book. The Collector's edition also includes a SteelBook case and a wearable replica Spartan helmet. All pre-orders get a "Specialist Pack" DLC.
- **Trailers:** Steam shows four: the Reveal Trailer, the Gameplay Reveal, the Renegade Gameplay Trailer and the Pre-Order Trailer.

## The story so far

The official site sets the scene. For 25 years, the last survivors of nuclear war have fought each other in the Metro tunnels under Moscow. Now a fanatical Spartan called Hunter has united them. His regime, the Novoreich, rules through propaganda and fear and is preparing a new war for the surface.

The main character is the Stranger, a loner haunted by violent nightmares who has lived outside the city. Events force him back into the ruins of Moscow and down into the Metro, the one place he swore he would never return to.

## How it connects to the books and earlier games

According to Deep Silver's FAQ, METRO 2039 has an original story from 4A Games, written together with Dmitry Glukhovsky, the author of the METRO novels. It isn't based on any one book. The FAQ also says it is the next METRO title with a new protagonist and cast, and calls it a good starting point for players new to the series.

The publisher describes the game as a mix of exploration, survival, combat and stealth. The FAQ adds that the thawing, irradiated surface is more dangerous than ever.

## PC details from the Steam listing

Steam lists achievements, Steam Cloud saves, full controller support and DualShock and DualSense controller support. Full audio is listed in English, French, German, Italian, Spanish, Japanese, Polish, Brazilian Portuguese, Simplified Chinese, Ukrainian and more. When we checked, the Steam requirements section said only that a 64-bit processor and operating system are required.

## What's still unconfirmed

- **Full PC requirements:** Steam doesn't list a processor, graphics card or memory yet.
- **Campaign length:** not stated by the publisher.
- **Performance:** we haven't played or benchmarked METRO 2039, and no tested build is available to us.
- **The date itself:** 4 February 2027 is the date shown on 26 November 2026. Release dates can still change.

## How to follow it

Use the Steam app for this game (ID 2590240) or the official METRO 2039 site. Older METRO games and their Redux versions are still on sale, so make sure the page you open is for METRO 2039.

